{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor immediately identified postpartum headache with gestational hypertension/eclampsia risk as a high-priority emergency and directed the family to call 120, providing explicit seizure first-aid and transport instructions. All eight responsibility-chain items were met without any serious or minor in-chain error. Multiple high-order points were triggered and meaningfully completed: HO1 (calm, firm communication reducing family conflict), HO2 (executable caregiver plan despite baby-care and fatigue barriers), HO3 (active discovery of blood-pressure values,抽搐 timing, and drug details), and HO4 (safe bounded closure with teach-back on escalation criteria). No important non-chain defect is present, and closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid.",
